<div class="col-xs-12">
      <h1>ACC Board of Trustees Elections</h1>
   </div>
	<div class="col-xs-12">
      <!-- ADD BANNER PHP -->
      <div id="page-banner">
               </div>
      <!-- END -->
   </div>
   <!-- Begin Page Menu Widget Loop -->
      <div class="col-xs-12 col-sm-9">
      

				<div id="post-18" class="post-18 page type-page status-publish hentry">

					<div class="entry-content" id="main-content">
						<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Under Texas law, Austin Community College is a separate political subdivision. It is responsible for conducting elections to elect members of the ACC Board of Trustees, to levy taxes, and for annexation issues.</p>
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Members of the Board of Trustees represent residents of the ACC taxing district. Trustees are elected at large for six-year terms to provide appropriate high-level guidance and leadership to ensure the College meets the needs of the communities served. The next Board of Trustees election is Tuesday, November 3, 2026. Places 1, 2, and 3 will be up for election.</p>
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The window to apply to run for the Board of Trustees in the November 2026 election is closed. The next election will be in November 2028; Places 4, 5, and 6 will be up for election. Check this page in the summer of 2028 for information for how to apply to run.</p>
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Click <strong><a href="https://offices.austincc.edu/community-and-government-affairs/acc-board-of-trustees-elections/candidates-for-the-acc-board-of-trustees-2026-election/">HERE</a></strong> to view the list of those who have applied to be on the ballot for the November 2026 election.</p>
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Click <strong><a href="https://austincc.edu/accvotes">HERE</a></strong> for information on how to register to vote in the November 2026 election.</p>
<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity" />
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Campaign Financial Reports</h2>
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">All approved candidates and members of the Board of Trustees must complete financial reporting required by Title 15 of the Texas Election Code regulating political funds and campaigns.</p>
<figure class="wp-block-table">
<table class="has-fixed-layout">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><a href="https://www.ethics.state.tx.us/data/filinginfo/schedules/s26uniform.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">2026 Filing Schedule for Reports Due in Connection with Elections Held on Uniform Election Dates</a></td>
<td></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><a href="https://ethics.state.tx.us/data/forms/coh/e_coh.pdf" data-type="link" data-id="https://ethics.state.tx.us/data/forms/coh/e_coh.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Candidate/Officeholder Campaign Finance Report</a></td>
<td><a href="https://www.ethics.state.tx.us/data/forms/coh/COH-local_ins26.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Instruction Guide</a></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><a href="https://www.ethics.state.tx.us/data/forms/coh/coh_uc-local.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Candidate/Officeholder Report of Unexpended Contributions</a></td>
<td><a href="https://www.ethics.state.tx.us/data/forms/coh/COHuc_local_ins26.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Instruction Guide</a></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The reports below are from current Board of Trustee members, candidates for the Board of Trustees, and political action committees who are involved in elections.</p>
